  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 239 AM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nAnother shortwave moves through on Thursday and brings another\nchance for thunderstorms in the morning (15-30%) and in the \nafternoon (30-50%). This activity will follow a similar\ntrajectory to today's convection and be primarily over SW MO. No\nwidespread thunderstorms or severe weather is expected. A\nseparate low pressure system will move through the Upper Midwest\non Friday and bring our best chance for rain (40-80%) as well \nas a Marginal risk (1/5) for severe weather. Highest rainfall \ntotals and best chance for rain will be mostly along and north\nof I-44 with the higher totals near 1\". Next chance for rain\nwill be Monday and Tuesday afternoons as a mid-level high\npressure system sits over the SE CONUS and ushers in moisture to\nthe eastern Ozarks. Both days feature ~20% chance for rain. \n\nTemperatures steadily decrease through the end of the week and\ninto the weekend as a cold front moves through after the rain on\nFriday. Thursday and Friday will still be warm as we sit in the\nlower 90s across the area. Then, Saturday through Monday we\nhangout in the 80s with lows in the 60s. Tuesday starts to get\nwarm again with daytime highs reaching the lower 90s once again.",
